! Configuration

The user-facing settings are under ''Control Panel > Settings > ProseMirror''.

!! Markdown-style input shortcuts

Set `$:/config/prosemirror/markdown-shortcuts` to `yes` to enable Markdown-style input rules. The default is `no`, including for Markdown-like content types. The setting changes how input is recognised; saved `text/vnd.tiddlywiki` content is still WikiText.

Enabled rules include Markdown-style headings, blockquotes, lists, code blocks, horizontal rules and common inline marks. Definition term and description triggers are part of these optional input rules.

!! Visual widget blocks

Set `$:/config/prosemirror/enable-widget-blocks` to `yes` to render supported widget or macro paragraphs as visual blocks. The default is `yes`. Source-backed fallback nodes still protect unsupported syntax.

`$:/config/prosemirror/widget-block/auto-focus` controls whether entering a widget block's source-edit mode automatically focuses its textarea. The default is `yes`.

!! Autocomplete triggers

Trigger values are TiddlyWiki string arrays, so multiple prefixes and prefixes containing non-ASCII characters are supported.

|!Type |!Default triggers |!Configuration tiddler |
|Links |`[[` `【【` |`$:/config/prosemirror/autocomplete/link-triggers` |
|Macros |`<<` `《《` |`$:/config/prosemirror/autocomplete/macro-triggers` |
|Transclusions |`{{` `「『` |`$:/config/prosemirror/autocomplete/transclusion-triggers` |
|Definition terms |`;` `；` |`$:/config/prosemirror/def-term-triggers` |
|Definition descriptions |`:` `：` |`$:/config/prosemirror/def-desc-triggers` |

!! Keyboard shortcuts

Shortcut overrides are stored at `$:/config/prosemirror/shortcuts/<action>`. Leave an override empty to use its default or set it to `none` to disable that binding. The settings tab exposes the principal formatting, history, heading, block and list shortcuts.

The shortcut syntax is the one accepted by `prosemirror-keymap`, for example `Mod-b`, `Shift-Ctrl-2` or `none`.
